Description: Set the avformat consumer running before starting its thread
 The encoding thread loops while the running property is set, but the property was only set after creating the thread. If the thread got to its loop first, it skipped encoding and marked the consumer stopped, and the start function then set running again, so the consumer looked like it was running forever. A thread failing early had the same effect. Set the property before creating the thread.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/mltframework/mlt/commit/75941cb426f3236c75a64f25e8a4c51e95680ac8
Author: Erich Seifert
Bug: https://github.com/mltframework/mlt/issues/1333
Applied-Upstream: master after v7.42.0, https://github.com/mltframework/mlt/pull/1366 (merged 2026-11-22 as be583ee302a26ea24d0a5ddb1ec01c5191063ec3)
Last-Update: 2026-11-26

diff --git a/src/modules/avformat/consumer_avformat.c b/src/modules/avformat/consumer_avformat.c
index 030b0b798..5122769c2 100644
--- a/src/modules/avformat/consumer_avformat.c
+++ b/src/modules/avformat/consumer_avformat.c
@@ -576,11 +576,11 @@ static int consumer_start(mlt_consumer consumer)
         // Assign the thread to properties
         mlt_properties_set_data(properties, "thread", thread, sizeof(pthread_t), free, NULL);
 
+        // Set the running state before the thread checks it
+        mlt_properties_set_int(properties, "running", 1);
+
         // Create the thread
         pthread_create(thread, NULL, consumer_thread, consumer);
-
-        // Set the running state
-        mlt_properties_set_int(properties, "running", 1);
     }
     return error;
 }
